%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f0d9b320ba1bccb4f9fd7e7f2cb4c281, type: 3}
  m_Name: Fake Bank Letter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScamCaseData
  caseId: C03
  queueNumber: A103
  caseTitle: Fake Bank Letter
  scamType: Investment Scam
  victimName: Alice Lee
  victimAge: 42
  victimOccupation: Operations Manager
  initialComplaint: Oh so sorry, I was lost in my worries, im Alice. Someone claiming
    to be a financial adviser contacted me about an investment opportunity that was
    supposedly offered through a major bank. They even showed me documents carrying
    the bank's branding.
  lobbyNpcPrefab: {fileID: 6377121035299240574, guid: 0475e43ff63f5a54fbf6d294e5fa7322, type: 3}
  interviewNpcPrefab: {fileID: 6377121035299240574, guid: 0475e43ff63f5a54fbf6d294e5fa7322, type: 3}
  behaviourType: 1
  receptionDialogue: Hi... thanks for seeing me. I received a security message about
    my bank account, and I'm worried someone may have gotten access to it.
  interviewDecisions:
  - npcLine: "I received this letter that looked like it came from my bank. It looked
      official, so I didn\u2019t really question it at first."
    choices: []
  - npcLine: The letter said there was a problem with my account and that I needed
      to verify some information urgently.
    choices:
    - playerChoice: What made the letter look genuine to you?
      npcResponse: "\u201CIt had the bank\u2019s logo, proper formatting, and even
        some of my personal details. It looked like the kind of letter a bank would
        actually send."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - bank_impersonation
      - fake_letterhead
      - bank_logo
    - playerChoice: You trusted him just because he said he worked for a bank?
      npcResponse: It wasn't just that. He showed me documents too, but I don't remember
        all the details.
      unlockedFactIds:
      - bank_impersonation
  - npcLine: The letter told me to scan a QR code and follow the instructions to
      verify my account.
    choices:
    - playerChoice: What happened after you scanned the QR code?
      npcResponse: "It opened a website that looked almost exactly like my bank\u2019s
        login page. I entered my username and password because I thought I was verifying
        my account."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - high_returns
      - limited_time_pressure
      - claimed_safe_investment
    - playerChoice: You entered your banking details from a QR code in a letter?
      npcResponse: "Yes\u2026 because everything looked connected. The letter, the
        logo, the website\u2014it all seemed official at the time."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - limited_time_pressure
  - npcLine: "After that, I started receiving alerts about activity on my account
      that I didn\u2019t recognise."
    choices:
    - playerChoice: What kind of activity did you notice?
      npcResponse: "There were login alerts and a transaction I definitely didn\u2019t
        make. That\u2019s when I contacted the bank directly."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - suspicious_transfer
      - not_official_bank_account
      - direct_bank_verification
    - playerChoice: You should have contacted the bank before scanning anything.
      npcResponse: "I know. I just didn\u2019t think it was fake until I saw the
        transaction."
      unlockedFactIds:
      - suspicious_transfer
  - npcLine: "I honestly thought the letter was real. If the bank logo and website
      can both be copied, I don\u2019t know what I\u2019m supposed to trust anymore."
    choices:
    - playerChoice: Be more careful next time, always check with the bank before
        doing anything potentially dangerous.
      npcResponse: Yeah, i will. Thanks
      unlockedFactIds: []
  howTheScamWorks: Scammers impersonate financial advisers or representatives of
    legitimate banks and offer fake investment opportunities. They may use fake letters,
    logos and other bank branding to make the offer appear genuine before convincing
    victims to transfer money.
  warningSigns: "\u2022 Unsolicited investment offers.\n\u2022 Pressure to invest
    quickly.\n\u2022 Promises of unusually high or guaranteed returns.\n\u2022 Bank-branded
    documents that cannot be independently verified.\n\u2022 Requests to transfer
    money to accounts that do not belong to the financial institution being represented."
  howToAvoid: Verify investment opportunities directly with the financial institution
    through official contact channels. Do not rely solely on documents, messages
    or contact information supplied by the person offering the investment.
  whatToDoIfVictim: Contact the relevant bank immediately if money has already been
    transferred. Preserve messages, documents and transaction records and report
    the incident through the appropriate official channels.
  caseFileParagraph:
  - textBefore: The victim received an
    dropdown:
      fieldId: 
      options: []
      correctOptionIndex: 0
      supportingFactId: 
  - textBefore: The letter contained
    dropdown:
      fieldId: 
      options: []
      correctOptionIndex: 0
      supportingFactId: 
  - textBefore: Believing the instructions were legitimate, she entered
    dropdown:
      fieldId: 
      options: []
      correctOptionIndex: 0
      supportingFactId: 
  - textBefore: This exposed her bank account to unauthorised access.
    dropdown:
      fieldId: 
      options: []
      correctOptionIndex: 0
      supportingFactId: 
  caseFileDropdowns:
  - fieldId: letter_instruction
    options:
    - Official-looking fake bank letter
    - Employment contract
    - Parcel collection notice
    - Telecommunications promotion
    correctOptionIndex: 0
    supportingFactId: fake_bank_letter
  - fieldId: 'information_provided '
    options:
    - Instructions to visit a bank branch
    - A QR code or link directing her to a fake banking website
    - A legitimate cheque
    - A customer-service phone number only
    correctOptionIndex: 1
    supportingFactId: fake_bank_link
  - fieldId: 
    options:
    - Only her mailing address
    - Her employment information
    - Her banking login credentials and verification information
    - A parcel tracking number
    correctOptionIndex: 2
    supportingFactId: bank_credentials
